  {
   "text": "His story was that he bought international reply coupons cheaply abroad and redeemed them at face value in the United States.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 8.06
  },
  {
   "text": "Between February and March 1920, the money invested rose from five thousand to twenty-five thousand dollars.",
   "start": 8.78,
   "end": 15.95
  },
  {
   "text": "By late July, Ponzi was taking in two hundred and fifty thousand dollars a day.",
   "start": 16.4,
   "end": 21.72
  },
  {
   "text": "But to cover the money, a hundred and sixty million coupons would have had to exist, and only about twenty-seven thousand did.",
   "start": 22.28,
   "end": 29.66
  }
 ]
